WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.502
-How y'all doing?
Look at this beautiful audience!

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:03.670
The energy!
-Come on. You feel that?

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.238
-Needed this! Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.806
-Right? We need it, right?
-It feels good.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.342
-We need that --
to recharge our batteries.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.944
-Yes. Feels nice
to be around people again.

00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:15.448
-I saw you, by the way. You did
a great job at the Emmys.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.783
You're on E!
on the red carpet now.

00:00:17.783 --> 00:00:19.252
-Yeah, yeah, you know
what I mean? I'm trying to get

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:21.454
to my little Ryan Seacrest gig
right quick,

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.089
you know what I mean? Step in.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.558
-You're fantastic at it.
Do you enjoy doing it?

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.293
-Listen, it was a dream of mine.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.794
I used to work
in social services.

00:00:28.794 --> 00:00:30.563
And I lived in Texas,

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.498
and I was a single father,
for anybody who doesn't know.

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:35.034
I could not afford
hosting classes.

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:38.104
And so I would mute my TV,

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:41.540
and when Ryan Seacrest,
Joan Rivers, Giuliana Rancic,

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.443
you know, the E! hosts were on,

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:47.146
and I would pretend, like,
using captions that I was them.

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:48.347
And to be there now --

00:00:48.347 --> 00:00:49.749
-Like, reading
like a teleprompter?

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.151
-Reading the teleprompter.
It was like me being at home,

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:55.521
the kids are doing homework,
and I'm like, "Today on E!,

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:56.589
we're gonna --"

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.625
And now, like --
And now here it is.

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.092
I tell this story,

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:01.994
because anybody out there
who has a dream,

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:04.097
literally, you might be
in a circumstance right now

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:05.731
where you feel like
you can't make it.

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:07.700
Just believe in yourself.
Keep practicing.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.835
Keep doing what you gotta to do.
And you can make it.

00:01:09.835 --> 00:01:10.904
It's the truth.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.238
-I love that.
-It's the truth.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.940
Yeah.
-That's a crazy story.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.441
-Yeah, it is.

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:17.143
-Did you bring anyone with you?

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.144
-I did. I brought my best friend
of 25 years.

00:01:19.144 --> 00:01:20.513
His name is Tre,
best friend Tre.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:23.016
And it was really hard
for me to get him.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:27.220
But we been homies since like
18 years old, college days,

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.122
and I was like, "If I'm having
this experience,

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.690
I want him to be there."
You know what I mean?

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.692
-Yeah.
-And I brought him, got him in,

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:34.760
and I said, "You got to look
like you doing something.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.429
So I'm giving you one job.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.030
Take photos of me
with these celebrities.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.299
These are some of
the icons of the icons."

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:42.569
-Yeah. And you can hang out,
go to the Emmys.

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:44.303
-Yeah.
-And all his job was to do --

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:46.005
just take photos
of you and the celebrities.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.273
-Take photos of me
and the celebrities.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.340
-You brought us some photos?

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.876
-I did. I mean, amazing photos.

00:01:50.876 --> 00:01:52.779
-Taken by Tre.
-By Tre.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:55.515
-Yeah, this is a great picture
of you with Angela Bassett.

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:57.049
-Angela Bassett, the queen.

00:01:57.049 --> 00:01:58.917
-Yeah, take a look.
-And if you can see,

00:01:58.917 --> 00:02:01.254
Tre clearly didn't understand
the assignment.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.689
-That's you,
and that's Angela Bassett.

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:05.424
-The bald head. Angela Bassett.

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:07.961
-Angela Bassett.
And there's Tre.

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.629
-There's Tre.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.297
-Oh, this is a good shot here.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.299
That is you and Cedric.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:15.101
-Cedric the Entertainer.
Y'all know Cedric.

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.468
-Ced, he's the best.
-He's one of the best

00:02:16.468 --> 00:02:17.870
of the best.
-You and Cedric the Entertainer.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.338
Here's just
a great photo of you.

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:21.073
-Yeah.
-And the Entertainer.

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:22.609
There you go. That's --

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:24.376
[ Applause ]

00:02:24.376 --> 00:02:25.578
-What'd I tell you?

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.981
I told Tre, "All your job is,

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:30.616
is to take photos
of me and the celebrities."

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:32.284
-That's it.
This one is my favorite one,

00:02:32.284 --> 00:02:36.322
because this is a picture
of you and Taraji P. Henson.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.423
-This -- He didn't even get me.

00:02:38.423 --> 00:02:39.959
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:41.461
♪♪

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:42.595
I appreciate that.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.463
There's literally a point
at the day, Jimmy,

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:46.866
that literally, he just said,
"Forget it. I'm just

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:49.068
going to start taking photos
of myself and the celebrities."

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:53.072
Like, he had 98 photos, no joke,
'cause I counted, on his phone,

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.374
and only 2 were of me in it.

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:56.576
Two.
-Tre?

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:57.944
-That was it.
-He's got a sense of humor.

00:02:57.944 --> 00:02:59.679
He's funny, man.
-Yeah, he is, he is.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:03.216
Well, you brought something that
I think is even a cooler thing,

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:05.017
which I appreciate
you saved for our show,

00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:08.554
because I was talking to you
about the E! red carpet,

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:11.023
and you were like hosting,
and you go, "Yeah."

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:13.392
I go, "When did you
get started doing this?"

00:03:13.392 --> 00:03:15.494
And you got a weird
opportunity, right?

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:17.263
You got into, what, modeling?

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:19.065
-Yeah, so, when I was
leaving social services,

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:21.501
I started to model,
try to host, as well.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:24.304
And I got this call, and they
were like, "You're working with,

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:26.839
like, a big celebrity. This
going to be, like, a big job."

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.274
And I was, like, freaking out.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:30.944
They wouldn't tell me
who it was, what it was.

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:32.578
They were like,
"You have to show up

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:35.214
and, you know, just get
hair and makeup ready,

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:36.615
and you're going to work
with this big celebrity,"

00:03:36.615 --> 00:03:38.150
and I'm freaking out.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.686
Get there. They start
putting makeup on me,

00:03:40.686 --> 00:03:42.755
and they're like,
"You're a zombie."

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:45.424
And I was like --
Seriously, a zombie.

00:03:45.424 --> 00:03:47.226
I was like, "I don't get it.
What do you mean?"

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:48.360
They're like, "Don't worry.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.096
The celebrity wants you
to be a zombie.

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:51.264
They want you to be a zombie."

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.665
-Like, "We need some
good-looking zombies."

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:55.234
-"We need some good-looking
zombies." And I was like --

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:57.837
I'm looking at the girl with me.
She's like 5'10" and gorgeous.

00:03:57.837 --> 00:04:00.506
I'm like, "Well, I guess
we're gonna be cute zombies.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.241
Okay, girl." Like, yeah.

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:05.611
We get there,
and it's literally Joan Rivers.

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:07.012
-Oh.
-The icon.

00:04:07.012 --> 00:04:08.013
-This is you.

00:04:08.013 --> 00:04:09.382
-No one has ever
seen these photos.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:13.052
I took selfies
where I'm a zombie

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.954
with Joan Rivers,

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.255
eating meat.

00:04:16.255 --> 00:04:17.557
-Dude, that is insane.

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:19.992
-This is one of my first
Hollywood jobs, again.

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:21.861
Like --
-I love that you --

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.830
-Look at this, Joan Rivers.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:24.897
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.565
-And how was Joan?
What was this for?

00:04:26.565 --> 00:04:28.167
-I have to tell you,
I had no idea what it was for,

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.036
because I never saw it anywhere.
-Really?

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:32.572
-Like, literally, we showed up
at her house. We took photos.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:34.841
She gave me a couple kisses
on the mouth.

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:37.876
Like, the best kiss ever,
while looking like that.

00:04:37.876 --> 00:04:39.245
-Yeah.
-And I was like,

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:40.413
"Girl, are you sure
you want to do this?"

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.481
-A zombie, yeah?
-Yeah. And --

00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:44.083
-Did she talk to you
or give you any advice?

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:46.419
-She did. She actually pulled me
to the side, and she was like,

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.821
"For you to have a sense of
humor to come here and do this,

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:51.256
you have a humility about you.

00:04:51.256 --> 00:04:52.725
Keep that. Keep going.

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:54.927
People are going to try to
break you down in this business.

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:56.429
Do not let them break you down.

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:59.264
Don't let no's stop you.
Let them propel you."

00:04:59.264 --> 00:05:01.601
I mean, she was just dropping
knowledge after knowledge.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:02.969
-Really?
-Yeah and I'm sitting there

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:04.771
in zombie makeup,
and I'm like, "Okay, Joan."

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:06.706
Yeah, whatever you want.
-Yeah. Yeah. Joan Rivers,

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.373
that's how you do it.
-Exactly, that's how you do it.

00:05:08.373 --> 00:05:09.508
You know what I mean?

00:05:09.508 --> 00:05:11.377
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:13.646
-I love her, man. I miss her.
-I do, too.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.914
-I do want to talk to you
about your acting role

00:05:15.914 --> 00:05:17.750
over in "Dear White People."
-Yeah.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:21.921
-You join the cast for
the season -- the final season.

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:23.956
-Yeah.
-How did you get the gig,

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.091
and did you always --

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:26.725
I mean, you're a good actor.

00:05:26.725 --> 00:05:28.828
-Oh, you know what, Jimmy?
Hold on!

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:30.696
-No, no, this is --
-Mama, we made it!

00:05:30.696 --> 00:05:32.731
-No, no, no. Come on. We --
-Okay, we --

00:05:32.731 --> 00:05:34.534
-We will see soon, in the clip.
-Okay, yeah.

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:36.836
-But that's great. I mean,
you just auditioned or --

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.971
-No, you know what?
I did audition,

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:40.806
but it was something
that in the back of my mind,

00:05:40.806 --> 00:05:43.109
I always wanted to do.
But I didn't tell anyone,

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:46.078
'cause sometimes people in our
lives have this unconscious fear

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:48.747
of stopping us
from going after what we want

00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:50.917
because they're afraid
to go after their own lives.

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:53.119
So I secretly studied,
did what I needed to do.

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:55.254
And then Justin Simien,

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:57.356
who's the creator of
"Dear White People," was like,

00:05:57.356 --> 00:06:00.493
"If you want to audition
and try it, here it goes."

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:03.863
And I auditioned just like
everyone else and got the role.

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:06.466
And luckily, it wasn't too far
away from what I do naturally.

00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:08.501
I'm playing a college counselor.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.536
So I'm still guiding people
and counseling them.

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:12.772
-Yeah, but, no, dude,
you're fantastic in it.

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:14.640
-Appreciate it, brother.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.508
Here's Karamo in
"Dear White People."

00:06:16.508 --> 00:06:17.777
Take a look at this.

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:21.214
-Harvard Medical
is well within your reach.

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:23.182
-Pathobiology
didn't ruin anything?

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:24.516
-You talking about
the "A"-minus?

00:06:24.516 --> 00:06:26.018
-Ugh.
-You kidding me, right?

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:29.221
You brought the class average
up to a --

00:06:29.221 --> 00:06:30.689
A "D"-plus.
-[ Sighs ]

00:06:30.689 --> 00:06:31.924
-Yeah, I got to get
a lot more people

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:33.192
to sign up for psych this year.

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:36.729
-Yeah, well, I was thinking
of adding something.

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:40.699
-Joelle, you are familiar with
the ancient art of sleeping.

00:06:40.699 --> 00:06:42.735
-Yes, but I guess I just wish

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:45.003
there was something on
my schedule worth waking up for.

00:06:45.003 --> 00:06:46.972
-Listen, you're no good
to anyone else,

00:06:46.972 --> 00:06:49.408
especially yourself,
if you're burnt out.

00:06:49.408 --> 00:06:51.910
If you have to add something,

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:54.247
go ahead
and add something that's fun.

00:06:54.247 --> 00:06:56.382
We all have a lot of needs.

00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:59.818
But, Joelle, being productive
is just one of them.

00:06:59.818 --> 00:07:01.120
-Yeah, we need --

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.289
I need more Karamo on my TV!

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:05.391
I want Karamo in the movies!

00:07:05.391 --> 00:07:07.259
Karamo, everybody!

00:07:07.259 --> 00:07:09.662
The final season
of "Dear White People"

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:11.364
is streaming now on Netflix.

